<Base title="Support & contact — fonecheck" description="Get in touch with Finnvek about fonecheck, the Android diagnostics app planned for fall 2026.">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-header"><p class="eyebrow">A human on the other end</p><h1>Let’s take a look.</h1><p class="lead">Have a question about fonecheck or something on this website? Get in touch.</p></header><div class="simple-page prose"><h2>Contact Finnvek</h2><a class="support-contact" href="mailto:contact@finnvek.com">contact@finnvek.com</a><p>For an app question, include your phone model, Android version and a short description of what you want to know. Please do not send passwords or other sensitive information.</p><h2>Before you download</h2><p>fonecheck is not yet available. It is planned for Google Play in fall 2026; an exact release date has not been announced.</p><p>You can <a href="/#explore">explore the app</a>, see the <a href="/#pricing">planned pricing</a> or read the <a href="/#faq">frequently asked questions</a> in the meantime.</p><h2>Understanding a result</h2><p>A missing test or an unavailable reading does not automatically mean a hardware fault. Start with the observation’s details and the report’s coverage. Our <a href="/guides/understanding-your-report/">report guide</a> explains how to read them together.</p></div></div>
</Base>
